  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile RNA models with scvi_n200 (config_005/006) achieve ~0.65 acc, far outperforming singleprofile and image-only baselines. Aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) appears negligible for scvi_n200 (0.650 vs 0.653). However, the scgpt encoder is completely untested, leaving open the question of whether a different RNA representation could further improve performance. Question: config_009 (scgpt, multiprofile, transformer) directly isolates the encoder effect by holding profile setting and aggregation constant relative to config_006, giving a clean scgpt-vs-scvi_n200 comparison in the strongest setting. Why this is the best next experiment: Before committing budget to multimodal fusion experiments (which add complexity and depend on choosing the best RNA encoder), we need to know whether scgpt offers a meaningful improvement over scvi_n200. If scgpt matches or beats scvi_n200 here, it reshapes the multimodal search; if it underperforms, we can confidently anchor multimodal experiments on scvi_n200. This single-variable test maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

